    <li><strong>GNT Road / NH-16 close by:</strong> the layout isn't far from GNT Road, one of North Chennai's main commuter and logistics roads.</li>
    <li><strong>Near the Red Hills lake:</strong> this belt sits close to the Red Hills lake, one of Chennai's key water sources — a reason people have settled and stayed in this area for years.</li>
    <li><strong>North Chennai is growing:</strong> road and industrial development in this part of the city has been pulling in more people and more demand for layouts around Sholavaram.</li>
    <li><strong>Part of the Ponneri-Gummidipoondi belt:</strong> Sholavaram falls in Ponneri Taluk, under CMDA administration. Ponneri itself is a marked node in the Chennai-Bengaluru Industrial Corridor (CBIC), and real estate activity in this belt is reported to be picking up alongside that industrial push.</li>
