<!-- 3C. WAYS BUYERS USE PLOTS HERE -->
<section id="value">
  <h2>What Buyers Do With Land in This Belt</h2>
  <p>You're buying an empty plot here — no construction, no rental figures tied to Plot 1 or Plot 2 specifically. But Sholavaram and Red Hills is a working industrial belt with real, steady demand for worker housing, and most buyers here go one of two ways with their land. Both make sense — it depends on what you're trying to do.</p>

  <h3>Build 1RK Rental Rooms — what most people here do</h3>
  <p>Factories and warehouses in Sholavaram/Red Hills run all year, and small 1RK rooms for rent to their workers stay in demand because of it. This is what most buyers end up building once the plot is in their name.</p>
  <div class="card-highlight mobile-only">
    <span class="hl-label">Typical rent per 1RK room</span>
    <span class="hl-num">₹3,000–4,000/mo</span>
  </div>
  <div class="table-label">Market context for a 1RK build <span class="estimate-tag">Local market estimate</span></div>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="kv-table">
      <!-- <caption>Market context for a 1RK build <span class="estimate-tag">Local market estimate</span></caption> -->
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Typical rent per 1RK room</th><td class="num">₹3,000–4,000/month</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Typical construction cost</th><td class="num">₹1,400–1,600/sq.ft</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Common demand source</th><td class="num">Factory &amp; warehouse workers</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--ink-soft);">These numbers show what's typical in the local market — they're not a yield promise for Plot 1 or Plot 2. How many rooms, what it'll cost, what rent you'll actually get — that depends on your plan, so check with a local contractor and during your visit.</p>

  <h3>Hold the Land, or Build Your Own House</h3>
  <p>A lot of buyers just hold the plot and let it sit — no tenant to manage, no repairs, nothing to think about except the yearly property tax once it's registered in your name. If you're planning for retirement, or want to put some money into land instead of FD, mutual funds, or gold, this is the simple, no-effort option. Some buyers also build their own house here, since it's close to where they work in the industrial belt.</p>
  <div class="note">
    <strong>Why patience matters with land, same as it does with a mutual fund or gold:</strong> the ones who put money into a fund or gold and don't touch it for years are usually the ones who see it work out. Land in a growing belt behaves the same way — it rewards people who hold, not people who panic and sell early. The owner of this layout bought and built his own house in this same belt about 7 years ago and still lives here today — that's not a return figure, just a real example of someone who chose to stay put. And the reasons to expect this belt to keep drawing more people aren't going away: the industrial companies around Sholavaram and Red Hills are only growing, and the Madhavaram Metro coming up nearby is pulling this side of Chennai closer to the rest of the city. None of this is a guarantee — land can also stay flat — but the timing and the direction here both look reasonable for someone willing to wait.
  </div>
  <p>If you're holding the plot with an eye on selling later, the question that matters is: what's this land worth in a few years? Same formula for both plots: <code class="fx">(future rate/sq.ft × plot size) − price you paid</code></p>
  <div class="table-label">Plot 1 vs Plot 2 — resale scenarios, side by side <span class="estimate-tag">Projection, not a guarantee</span></div>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="compact-table plot-compare-table">
      <caption>Plot 1 vs Plot 2 — resale scenarios, side by side <span class="estimate-tag">Projection, not a guarantee</span></caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th rowspan="2">Scenario</th>
          <th rowspan="2" class="num">Rate/sq.ft</th>
          <th colspan="2">Plot 1 — 1,096 sq.ft (₹26,30,400 paid)</th>
          <th colspan="2">Plot 2 — 1,231 sq.ft (₹29,54,400 paid)</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="num">Resale value</th><th class="num">Gain</th>
          <th class="num">Resale value</th><th class="num">Gain</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
